## Integration

* Reuse Viroopa request/calendar, strict JSON, complete source collector,
  compiler and verified-persistence workflow. Only the workflow's compiler
  argument is adapted to the canonical branch name; compiler functions do not change.
* Accept the entire positive request grammar with either the historical
  `for PowerTools at ...` or current `for ...` branch phrase. No trailing
  instructions, identity claims, traversal or malformed date headers are accepted.
* Bind a branch by exact full name/suffix, or unique containment of meaningful
  query words in observed store names. Generic shop descriptors alone do not
  identify a branch; ambiguous/unknown qualifiers decline before writes.
  This adapter is local to the export and does not change find_store.
* Compare reviewed AGENTS prose exactly after whitespace normalization, allowing
  only its six declared /proc roots and two yes/no answer tokens to vary.
  Security and availability policy prose remains exact. Full source/policy bytes,
  identity and date are revalidated before the Write attempt.
* Preserve one-Write / exact-readback / terminal-post-Write-uncertainty semantics.
  Only a readback-confirmed file receives OUTCOME_OK and the bare path answer.

The parent's WORLD cache classifies by the first record in each source subtree,
silently skips failed reads, and sets built before collection completes. It cannot
prove the completeness required for a family export. Therefore this version uses
the existing Viroopa complete two-scan collector instead of treating WORLD as
complete evidence. This is an explicit design refinement to the proposed index
reuse; no new collection algorithm was invented.

## Reproduce

Use Python 3.12 and pydantic-monty==1.2.0 in an isolated environment:

```sh
python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install pydantic-monty==1.2.0
.venv/bin/python build.py
.venv/bin/python verify.py
```

upstream/ contains exact Brain exports with the `viroopa__NAME_EXT` logical names.
build.py verifies donor hashes, preserves parent/compiler ASTs, uses the shared
lzpack packer, independently decodes and checks AST identity, and enforces the
65,536-byte source cap. readable.py is the review source; agent.py is the exact
runnable packed artifact. No live model or ECOM call occurs during reproduction.

## Evidence and limits

143 inherited contract controls (73 pure, 21 collection, 49 workflow); independent
datetime checks on 3,456 dates; independent CSV arithmetic on 250 random worlds /
20,489 cells; 16 whole-agent non-target comparisons including exact model requests;
7 branch cases; 3 semantic policy changes. Five native Monty scenarios execute
the exact packed bytes with fake SDK bindings, including persistence failures.
See offline_results.json for exact results and timings.

Viroopa's archived complete world retains 118 real Read pairs. Reconstructed Lists
and simulated persistence reproduce the old recorded CSV. A second test uses the
current record's actual request, AGENTS, security, clock and identity with the
older archived catalogue/inventory. It proves adapter applicability and checks
the resulting CSV against an independent oracle; it is not a replay of current
live source data and establishes no current live grade.

On that archive the supported path uses 297 simulated RPCs, zero model calls,
one Write, and about 0.21 seconds of local Monty-plus-fake-host wall time. This
is not a network latency or live cost measurement. Non-target packing overhead
does not add model/tool calls. Unknown policy variants, identities other than
RoleEmployee, unsupported layouts/phrases or bounded-collection failures decline.
Two scans are not atomic; Stat-then-Write has an inherent concurrent-creator race.
No speculative extra scans, generic verifiers or unrelated riders are included.
